      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose is above the maximum.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg/day**. The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg/day**, which is 850 mg three times daily. For extended-release, the maximum is 2000 mg/day. This order is double the highest allowed dose, which raises the risk of severe GI side effects and lactic acidosis.\n\n**What may have been meant:**\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum), if \"1700\" was a mix-up between the unit dose and the daily dose\n- **1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- Something else, such as a lower starting dose like 500 mg twice daily, if this is a new start\n\nCould you confirm the dose, frequency and formulation (IR or ER)? I'll enter it once you do. If you do want a dose above the labeled maximum, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note on the order."
      }
